  <static seed="104" source="Library/272/setStewart12_5/problem_10.pg">
    <statement><p>Find an equation of a plane through the point (0, 5, -4)
which is orthogonal to the line 
<me>x = -2 + 1t, \quad y = 1
+ 2t, \quad  z = 1  - 2t</me> in which the coefficient of 
<m>x</m> is 1.</p>
<p>Equation: <fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0001"/> = 0.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1\mathopen{}\left(x-0\right)+2\mathopen{}\left(y-5\right)+\left(-2\right)\mathopen{}\left(z-\left(-4\right)\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
